# Hosts that reject GitHub-hosted runners rather than being genuinely broken.
# Verified by hand: each returns 200 from a normal client but fails from CI, so
# checking them produces a weekly false-positive report instead of signal.
# Re-test before removing an entry — these are environment quirks, not permanent truths.

# asciinema.org times out from GitHub-hosted runners (it answers in under a second from a
# normal connection). Raising --timeout to 30 and --max-retries to 3 in check-links.yml did
# not help, so this is an environment quirk rather than a slow host. The two recording URLs
# in README.md were timing out every run, burying the real errors in the weekly report.
# Re-test by dropping this entry and watching one scheduled run.
https://asciinema\.org/.*
